<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Getting Started with Node.js on Build</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <main class="container">
    <header>
      <div class="badge">⬢ Running on Build</div>
      <h1><%= greeting %></h1>
      <p class="subtitle">
        This is a sample Node.js + Express app deployed on
        <strong>Build</strong>. Clone it, change it, and redeploy —
        it's your playground.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Runtime info</h2>
      <table>
        <tr><th>Environment</th><td><%= env.nodeEnv %></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Node version</th><td><%= env.nodeVersion %></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Listening on port</th><td><%= env.port %></td></tr>
        <tr><th>Instance</th><td><%= env.instance %></td></tr>
      </table>
      <p class="hint">
        The port comes from the <code>PORT</code> environment variable that
        Build injects at runtime.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Live config vars</h2>
      <p>
        The greeting above is read from the <code>GREETING</code> config var.
        Change it without redeploying:
      </p>
      <pre><code>bld config:set GREETING="こんにちは, Build!" -a &lt;your-app&gt;</code></pre>
      <p>Then refresh this page, or hit the API:</p>
      <pre><code>curl https://&lt;your-app&gt;.build.io/api/greeting</code></pre>
      <p class="hint" id="api-result">Fetching <code>/api/status</code>…</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card">
      <h2>Make it yours</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <code>server.js</code> and uncomment the sample route at the bottom.</li>
        <li>Edit this page in <code>views/index.ejs</code>.</li>
        <li>Commit, push to GitHub, and watch Build redeploy automatically.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <footer>
      <a href="https://build.io">build.io</a> ·
      <a href="/api/status">/api/status</a> ·
      <a href="/api/greeting">/api/greeting</a>
    </footer>
  </main>

  <script>
    fetch('/api/status')
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(d => {
        document.getElementById('api-result').textContent =
          `Live from /api/status — status: ${d.status}, uptime: ${d.uptimeSeconds}s, node: ${d.node}`;
      })
      .catch(() => {
        document.getElementById('api-result').textContent =
          'Could not reach /api/status';
      });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
